speechtext:
Mr. Speaker, there have been consultations with the Opposition House Leaders, and I think you will find a predisposition to accept the following order of reference motion at this time by unanimous consent. The motion is as follows:
That the Standing Committee on Communications and Culture be empowered to study all aspects of copyright revision;
That the document entitled "From Gutenburg to Telidon, A White Paper on Copyright: Proposals for the Revision of the Canadian Copyright Act", tabled
Business of the House
earlier this day, be referred to the Committee and that the Committee examine and report upon the proposals contained therein;
That the Committee be empowered to retain expert staff; and That the Committee report its Findings and recommendations no later than May 24, 1985.
